    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d212">

                <pb facs="0293" n="281" sameAs="frus:frus1942v01/pg281"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">390.1115A/959: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Calcutta</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Schnare</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Calcutta</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-07-14T12:00:00+05:30">July 14,
                        1942—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 12:09 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>506. Your 301, July 3, 9 p.m. Estimate resident Americans now desiring
                    transportation between two and three hundred. VG<anchor n="47" xml:id="d212-f1"
                    /> and convalescent Army personnel may add about 200. Further Allied reverses
                    may increase evacuation resident Americans. Please advise what shipping
                    facilities arranged.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schnare</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d212-f1" n="47" xml:id="d212-f1-content">
                <p>American Volunteer Group.</p>
            </note>
